    "rules": {
      "reading_surface_moves": false,
      "loop": "ambient-only",
      "ambient": "Ambient loops are allowed only in the home Switchboard hero and the pulsing status dots: slow, continuous, never moving text the reader is reading; lists and copy stay still. The home headline may rise in once on load; pointer micro-interactions respond to the pointer and never run on their own. Everything else reveals once and settles. Under prefers-reduced-motion ambient motion stops on its final frame.",
      "reduced_motion": "All transitions become instant; reveals render their settled final frame; ambient loops stop.",
      "source": "reveal durations and settled-still reduced motion from kit-06 rule motion-reveal; the kit's no-loop rule is narrowed to ambient-only by DEC-20261025-A; other durations and easings derived"
    }
